tee of the Board on HR 8. Committee for monitoring High Value NPAs & Loss Assets 9. Board Committee for Performance evaluation of Managing Director & CEOs/Executive Directors/ Chief General Managers/General Managers\n- 1 0 Banking\nबैैंक ऑҰफ़ इंडिया / BANK OF INDIA वािर््षक रिपोर््ट / Annual Report 2025-26\nFull Name of\nSr. No\nAppointment\nMembership in Committees of the\nNo of shares\nNumber of Membership of ACB & SRC\nNumber of Chairmanship of ACB & SRC\nArea of Expertise\nthe Director, Designation &\nDate\nBank $\nheld\nCategory\nin Public Ltd.\nin Public Ltd.\nCompanies including the\nCompanies including the\nBank\nBank\n9. Smt. Jamuna Ravi Shareholder Director (Non-Executive, Independent Director)","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c457","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":124,"text":"9. Smt. Jamuna Ravi Shareholder Director (Non-Executive, Independent Director)\n04.12.2025 1. Audit Committee of the Board 2. Stakeholder Relationship Committee 3. Share Transfer Committee 4. Special Committee of the Board for Monitoring and Follow up Cases of Fraud 5. Risk Management Committee 6. IT Strategy & Digital Payment Promotion Committee 7. Nomination & Remuneration Committee 8. Independent Directors Committee of the Board 9. Corporate Social Responsibility Committee 10. Board Committee for Performance evaluation of Managing Director & CEOs/Executive Directors/ Chief General Managers/General Managers 11. Group Governance Unit Committee\n500 1 1 IT\n205 0 1 Banking\n10. Shri Prabodh Parikh Shareholder Director (Non- Executive Independent Director)\n29-11-2025 1. Management Committee of the Board 2. Directors Promotion Committee 3. Disciplinary Proceedings Committee of the Board 4. Share Transfer Committee 5. Special Committee of the Board for Monitoring and Follow up Cases of Fraud 6. Risk Management Committee 7. Committee of Directors for Customer Service 8. IT Strategy & Digital Payment Promotion Committee 9. Nomination & Remuneration Committee 10. Steering Committee of the Board on HR\n11. Review Committee of Wilful Defaulters 12. Independent Directors Committee of the Board 13. Corporate Social Responsibility Committee 14. Group Governance Unit Committee","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c458","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":124,"text":"11. Review Committee of Wilful Defaulters 12. Independent Directors Committee of the Board 13. Corporate Social Responsibility Committee 14. Group Governance Unit Committee\nNote: 1. No Director of the Bank was a member in more than 10 committees or acted as Chairperson of more than 5 Committees across all listed entities/public limited companies in which he/she was a Director during the year 2025-26.\nबैैंक ऑҰफ़ इंडिया / BANK OF INDIA वािर््षक रिपोर््ट / Annual Report 2025-26\n2. There is no inter-se relationship between Directors. 3. The Board of Directors has been responsible for the business and overall affairs of the Bank in the FY 2025-26 and that the reporting structures of the Bank, formal and informal are in consistent with the same. 4. In the opinion of the Board, the independent directors fulfil the conditions specified in SEBI (LODR) regulations, 2015 and are independent of the management. 5. During FY 2025-26, there has been no instance of resignation by any of the Independent Directors.","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c459","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":125,"text":"All Directors, other than the Managing Director & CEO and the Executive Directors, are non-Executive Directors on the Board. Two Directors representing shareholders of the Bank other than the Central Government and one Part-time non-official Director are Independent directors within the meaning of Regulation 16(b) of SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015 (SEBI-LODR).\nDetails of familiarization programmes imparted to Independent Directors are available at https://bankofindia.bank.in/familirization.\nIn the opinion of the Board, independent directors fulfil the conditions specified in these Regulations and are independent of the Management.\nCommittee Membership of Directors :\nIn terms of regulations 26(1) of SEBI (LODR) Regulations, 2015, Chairpersonship and Membership of Audit Committee of the Board (ACB) and Stakeholders Relationship Committee (SRC) are considered for this disclosure.\nDetails of positions held by the Directors on the Committees of the Bank and unlisted/other listed/public limited companies where he/she was a Director as on 31.03.2026 are as given here under:\nName & Designation of\nMember\nSr. No\nName of the Company Name of the Committee (ACB/SRC)\nDirector\nACB, SRC Member\n1. Shri M.R. Kumar (Non-Executive Chairman)\n1.Bank of India 2.Cholamandalam Investment and Finance Co. Ltd. 3.Aurobindo Pharma Ltd.\nACB, SRC Member","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c460","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":125,"text":"ACB, SRC Member\n2. Shri Rajneesh Karnatak (MD & CEO)\n1.Bank of India 2.EXIM Bank 3.Indian Institute of Banking & Finance\n3. Shri P.R. Rajagopal (Executive Director)\n1.Bank of India 2.BOI Merchant Bankers Ltd. SRC, ACB Member\nSRC Member\n4. Shri Subrat Kumar (Executive Director)\n1.Bank of India 2.BOI Investment Managers P Ltd. 3.BOI Services Ltd., 4.Indo Zambia Bank Ltd.\nSRC Member\n5. Shri Rajiv Mishra (Executive Director)\n1.Bank of India 2.STCI Finance Ltd., 3.Star Union Daichi Life Insurance Co.Ltd.\n6. Shri Pramod Kumar Dwibedi (Executive Director)\n1.Bank of India 2.MPCon Ltd. SRC Member\nACB Member\n7. Shri Manoj M. Ayyappan (Non-Executive Director)\n1.Bank of India 2.NCGTC, Small Industries Development Bank of India\n8. Shri Ashok Narain (Non-Executive Director)\n1.Bank of India 2.Star Union Daichi Life Insurance Co.Ltd. ACB Member\n1.Bank of India ACB, SRC Chairperson - ACB\n9. Smt Jamuna Ravi (Non-Executive Director)\nMember- SRC\n10. Shri Prabodh Parikh Bank of India SRC Chairperson\nThe profiles of the directors who were appointed / nominated on the Board of the Bank and assumed office during the financial year 2025-26 are furnished hereunder:\nShri Pramod Kumar Dwibedi (Executive Director)\nShri Pramod Kumar Dwibedi has been appointed as Executive Director of Bank of India and assumed charge on 24.11.2025.","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c461","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":125,"text":"Shri Pramod Kumar Dwibedi has been appointed as Executive Director of Bank of India and assumed charge on 24.11.2025.\nShri Dwibedi, aged 58 Years, is a postgraduate in Economics & MBA (Finance) started his career in Banking in the year 1995 as Probationary Officer. He is certified Associate Member of Indian Institute of Bankers (CAIIB). He also holds a certification in IT and Cyber Security from the Institute for Development and Research in Banking Technology (IDRBT) for Senior Management and Fundamentals of Risk Management from Institute of Risk Management, London. In a career spanning over 30 years, he has worked in different capacities and has worked across the country and abroad. He has functioned in almost all areas of banking operations and Administrative offices. He\nबैैंक ऑҰफ़ इंडिया / BANK OF INDIA वािर््षक रिपोर््ट / Annual Report 2025-26\nsuccessfully handled responsibilities as General Manager, FGMO Bhopal, comprising of Madhya Pradesh & Chhattisgarh and as a Chief General Manager, FCGMO Pune.\nShri Prabodh Parikh (Shareholder Director)\nShri Prabodh Parikh, aged 63 years, is a post graduate in M.Com, M.B.A and is a Certified Associate of Indian Institute of Bankers (CAIIB). He joined State Bank of India (SBI) in 1985 and retired as Deputy Managing Director in 2023. He has 37 years of rich banking experience and has specialized in Infrastructure and Project financing.","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c462","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":126,"text":"He was nominated as Director by SBI on the board of Oman India Joint Investment Fund - Trustee Company Private Limited, Oman India Joint Investment Fund – Management Company Private Limited and SBI Infra Management Solutions Pvt. Ltd.\nHe was on deputation at NaBFID as Executive Vice President – Officer on Special Duty – looking after all the aspects to set up necessary infrastructure and kick starting the operations of NaBFID and business development.\nCessation: The following members ceased to be the Directors during the financial year 2025-26:\nSr.No. Name of Director Category Date of Cessation Reason 1. Shri Vishwanath V Shenoy Shareholder Director 28-11-2025 Completion of tenure\nConduct of Board Meetings:\nDuring the FY 2025-26, 20 (Twenty) Board Meetings were held on the following dates:\n25-04-2025 30-04-2025 09-05-2025 30-05-2025 26-06-2025 28-07-2025 29-07-2025 26-08-2025 26-09-2025 17-10-2025 30-10-2025 01-11-2025 28-11-2025 16-12-2025 30-12-2025 21-01-2026 27-01-2026 27-02-2026 16-03-2026 27-03-2026\nDetails of attendance of the Directors at the Board Meetings in FY 2025-26 are as follows:","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c463","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":126,"text":"Details of attendance of the Directors at the Board Meetings in FY 2025-26 are as follows:\nDirectors Name Total no. of meetings No. of meetings attended Period From To Rajneesh Karnatak 20 20 01-04-2025 31-03-2026 P. R. Rajagopal 20 17 01-04-2025 31-03-2026 Subrat Kumar 20 19 01-04-2025 31-03-2026 Rajiv Mishra 20 18 01-04-2025 31-03-2026 Pramod Kumar Dwibedi 8 8 24-11-2025 31-03-2026 Manoj M Ayyappan 20 14 01-04-2025 31-03-2026 Ashok Narain 20 20 01-04-2025 31-03-2026 Jamuna Ravi 20 20 01-04-2025 31-03-2026 *V V Shenoy 13 13 01-04-2025 28-11-2025 M R Kumar 20 20 01-04-2025 31-03-2026 Prabodh Parikh 7 7 29-11-2025 31-03-2026 * V V Shenoy ceased to be member during the year\nBoard Committees\nThe Board of Directors of the Bank has constituted various Committees of Directors to look into different areas of strategic importance in terms of Reserve Bank of India / SEBI / Government of India Guidelines on Corporate Governance and Risk Management. The Board Committees are as under:","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c464","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":126,"text":"The Board of Directors of the Bank has constituted various Committees of Directors to look into different areas of strategic importance in terms of Reserve Bank of India / SEBI / Government of India Guidelines on Corporate Governance and Risk Management. The Board Committees are as under:\nSr. No Name of the Committee 1. Management Committee of the Board 2. Audit Committee of the Board 3. Directors Promotion Committee 4. Disciplinary Proceeding Committee 5. Stakeholders’ Relationship Committee 6. Share Transfer Committee 7. Special Committee of the Board for Monitoring & Follow Up Cases for Frauds 8. Risk Management Committee 9. Committee of Directors for Customer Services 10. IT Strategy and Digital Payment Promotion Committee\nबैैंक ऑҰफ़ इंडिया / BANK OF INDIA वािर््षक रिपोर््ट / Annual Report 2025-26\n11. Nomination and Remuneration Committee of Directors 12. Credit Approval Committee of the Board 13. Steering Committee of the Board on HR 14. Review Committee for Willful Defaulters 15. Committee for Monitoring High Value NPAs and Loss Assets 16. Independent Directors’ Committee of the Board 17. Corporate Social Responsibility Committee 18. Committee for Performance Evaluation of MD&CEO, Executive Directors and General Managers 19. Group Governance Unit Committee\n1. The Management Committee of the Board","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c465","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":127,"text":"1. The Management Committee of the Board\nThe Management Committee of the Board is constituted as per the provisions of the Nationalised Banks (Management & Miscellaneous Provision) Scheme, 1970. The Management Committee exercises all the powers vested in the Board in respect of financial sanctions, compromises/write off proposals and filing of suits/appeals, etc. As on 31.03.2026, it comprised of 7 members consisting of MD & CEO, 4 Executive Directors and One Shareholder Director and One RBI Nominee Director.\nThe Management Committee of the Board met 26 times during the FY 2025-26 on the following dates:\n30-04-2025 13-05-2025 22-05-2025 30-05-2025 13-06-2025 24-06-2025 10-07-2025 24-07-2025 06-08-2025 25-08-2025 10-09-2025 17-09-2025 25-09-2025 09-10-2025 23-10-2025 19-11-2025 28-11-2025 12-12-2025 20-12-2025 30-12-2025 16-01-2026 27-01-2026 09-02-2026 26-02-2026 10-03-2026 23-03-2026\nDetails of attendance of the Directors at the Management Committee of the Board Meetings in FY 2025-26 are as follows:\nDirectors Name Meetings held during\nAttendance","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c466","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":127,"text":"Attendance\nPeriod From To Rajneesh Karnatak 26 26 01-04-2025 31-03-2026 P. R. Rajagopal 26 20 01-04-2025 31-03-2026 Subrat Kumar 26 25 01-04-2025 31-03-2026 Rajiv Mishra 26 23 01-04-2025 31-03-2026 Pramod Kumar Dwibedi 10 9 24-11-2025 31-03-2026 Ashok Narain 26 25 01-04-2025 31-03-2026 *V V Shenoy 17 16 01-04-2025 28-11-2025 Prabodh Parikh 9 9 29-11-2025 31-03-2026\ntheir tenure\nRecorded\n* V V Shenoy ceased to be member during the year\n2. Credit Approval Committee of the Board: In terms of the directions of the Government of India, Ministry of Finance, Department of Financial Services, New Delhi, vide their communication reference No.13/1/2006-130.1 dated 31st January 2012, the Bank has constituted the Credit Approval Committee of the Board. The Credit Approval Committee shall exercise the powers of the Board in respect of any single credit proposal upto Rs.800 Crore in case of our Bank and exposure exceeding such limits shall be considered by the Management Committee.\nThe members of the Committee are the Managing Director & CEO, the Executive Directors, The General Manager in-charge of Finance, CGM / General Manager in-charge of Risk Management and CGM/General Manager in charge of Credit. The Committee meetings are being chaired by the Managing Director & CEO of the Bank. Credit Approval Committee of the Board met 47 times during the FY 2025-26 on the following dates:","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c467","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":127,"text":"04-04-2025 09-04-2025 16-04-2025 02-05-2025 08-05-2025 16-05-2025 22-05-2025 31-05-2025 06-06-2025 12-06-2025 19-06-2025 25-06-2025 04-07-2025 15-07-2025 24-07-2025 31-07-2025 07-08-2025 14-08-2025 21-08-2025 28-08-2025 10-09-2025 19-09-2025 22-09-2025 25-09-2025 06-10-2025 16-10-2025 23-10-2025 30-10-2025 18-11-2025 27-11-2025 04-12-2025 11-12-2025 18-12-2025 26-12-2025 01-01-2026 08-01-2026 14-01-2026 22-01-2026 29-01-2026 05-02-2026 11-02-2026 18-02-2026 25-02-2026 05-03-2026 13-03-2026 24-03-2026 31-03-2026\nबैैंक ऑҰफ़ इंडिया / BANK OF INDIA वािर््षक रिपोर््ट / Annual Report 2025-26\n3. Audit Committee of the Board: The Audit Committee of the Board (ACB) has been constituted by the Board of Directors as per the guidelines of the Reserve Bank of India, the Government of India and Securities and Exchange Board of India Regulations as amended from time to time. The ACB provides direction and also oversees the operation of the total audit function of the Bank.\nAs on 31.03.2026, the Audit Committee comprises of 3 members viz. Shareholder Director, Government Nominee Director and Reserve Bank of India Nominee Director.\nUnaudited quarterly results of the Bank and audited results for the year were reviewed by the Audit Committee of the Board prior to placing before the Board of Directors for approval.\nDuring the FY 2025-26, the Audit Committee met 17 times on the following dates.","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c468","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":128,"text":"During the FY 2025-26, the Audit Committee met 17 times on the following dates.\n22-04-2025 09-05-2025 20-05-2025 05-06-2025 26-06-2025 17-07-2025 29-07-2025 13-08-2025 17-09-2025 09-10-2025 17-10-2025 19-11-2025 18-12-2025 16-01-2026 21-01-2026 16-02-2026 18-03-2026\nDetails of attendance of the Directors at the Audit Committee of the Board Meetings in FY 2025-26 are as follows:\nDirectors Name Meetings held during\nAttendance\nPeriod From To Jamuna Ravi 17 17 01-04-2025 31-03-2026 Manoj M Ayyappan 17 17 01-04-2025 31-03-2026 Ashok Narain 17 17 01-04-2025 31-03-2026\ntheir tenure\nRecorded\n4. Stakeholders Relationship Committee:\nIn compliance of Regulation 20 of SEBI (LODR) Regulations, 2015, Stakeholders’ Relationship Committee, has been constituted, for redressal of the grievances of the shareholders/ investors with regard to the transfer / transmission of shares, non-receipt of Balance Sheet, non-receipt of dividends, etc. All the references/ complaints received from the investors during the year have been replied / redressed till date. Investors’ grievances are normally attended to within seven days on receipt of the relevant information. The Committee comprises of Four Executive Directors and Two Shareholder Directors of the Bank.","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c469","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":128,"text":"During the year 2025-26, Bank has received 32 Complaints. All of these complaints have been resolved. The Committee met 4 times during the FY 2025-26 on the following dates:\n19-04-2025 08-08-2025 17-12-2025 10-02-2026\nThe attendance record of the members in the above meeting is shown below:\nDirectors Name Meetings held during\nAttendance\nPeriod From To P. R. Rajagopal 4 4 01-04-2025 31-03-2026 Subrat Kumar 4 4 01-04-2025 31-03-2026 Rajiv Mishra 4 4 01-04-2025 31-03-2026 Pramod Kumar Dwibedi 2 2 24-11-2025 31-03-2026 *V V Shenoy 2 2 01-04-2025 28-11-2025 Jamuna Ravi 4 4 01-04-2025 31-03-2026 Prabodh Parikh 2 2 29-11-2025 31-03-2026\ntheir tenure\nRecorded\n* V V Shenoy ceased to be member during the year\n5. Share Transfer Committee:\nIn terms of Bank of India (Shares & Meetings) Regulations, 2007 meeting of this committee is to be held as and when necessary. The committee comprises of Managing Director & CEO or in his absence any Executive Director and two Shareholder Directors. The Committee met 4 times during the FY 2025-26 on the following dates:\n19-04-2025 08-08-2025 17-12-2025 10-02-2026\n6. Risk Management Committee of the Board:","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c470","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":128,"text":"6. Risk Management Committee of the Board:\nThe Bank has evolved suitable risk management policies consistent with the SEBI guidelines, size of the Bank, level of complexity, risk profile and scope of operation of the Bank. Risk Management Committee was formed to review and evaluate the overall risks assumed by the Bank.\nबैैंक ऑҰफ़ इंडिया / BANK OF INDIA वािर््षक रिपोर््ट / Annual Report 2025-26\nThe committee consists of MD & CEO of the Bank any one Executive Director, and Two Shareholder Directors. Other Executive Directors are invitees. The Committee met 14 times during the FY 2025-26 on following dates:\n22-04-2025 19-05-2025 10-06-2025 24-06-2025 10-07-2025 13-08-2025 25-09-2025 15-10-2025 18-11-2025 11-12-2025 20-12-2025 16-01-2026 10-02-2026 16-03-2026\nThe attendance record of the members in the above meeting is shown below:\nDirectors Name Meetings held during\nAttendance\nPeriod From To Rajneesh Karnatak 14 13 01-04-2025 31-03-2026 P.R. Rajagopal 14 11 01-04-2025 31-03-2026 Jamuna Ravi 14 14 01-04-2025 31-03-2026 *V V Shenoy 9 9 01-04-2025 28-11-2025 Prabodh Parikh 5 5 29-11-2025 31-03-2026\ntheir tenure\nRecorded\n* V V Shenoy ceased to be member during the year\n7. Committee of Directors for Customer Service:","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c471","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":129,"text":"7. Committee of Directors for Customer Service:\nAs per the RBI guidelines, the Customer Service Committee of the Board was formed in September 2004. The functions of the Committee are to bring about improvement in the quality of customer service provided by the Bank on an ongoing basis and to review the performance of the Standing Committee on Customer Service (at the Head Office). It comprises of Whole Time Directors, GOI Nominee Director, one Shareholder’s Director. The Committee met 4 times during the FY 2025-26 on following dates:\n17-07-2025 06.09.2025 17.12.2025 09-03-2026\n8. Nomination and Remuneration Committee:\nUnder the provisions of Section 9 (3) (i) of Banking Companies (Acquisition and Transfer of Undertakings) Act, 1970, the Reserve Bank of India has laid down ‘Fit and Proper’ criteria to be fulfilled by the persons to be elected as Directors on the Boards of the Nationalised Banks. The Committee was formed in terms of Reserve Bank of India Notification No: RBI/DBR/2019-20/71/ Master Direction DBR-Appl. No: 9/29.67.001/2019-20 dated August 2, 2019. The NRC consists of Three Independent Director of the Bank. The Committee met four times during the FY 2025-26 on following dates:\n19-04-2025 27-10-2025 30-12-2025 27-02-2026\nDirectors Name Meetings held during\nAttendance","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c472","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":129,"text":"Attendance\nPeriod From To M R Kumar 4 4 01-04-2025 31-03-2026 Jamuna Ravi 4 4 01-04-2025 31-03-2026 *V V Shenoy 2 2 01-04-2025 28-11-2025 Prabodh Parikh 2 2 29-11-2025 31-03-2026 * V V Shenoy ceased to be member during the year\ntheir tenure\nRecorded\n9. Special Committee of the Board for Monitoring and Follow up cases of frauds\nThe Committee was formed to monitor large value frauds. This Committee consist of Non Executive Chairman of the Bank, Managing Director & CEO, Executive Directors, Government Nominee Director and two Shareholder Director. The Committee met 4 times during the FY 2025-26 on following dates:\n10-06-2025 06-09-2025 29-11-2025 10-03-2026\n10. IT Strategy and Digital Payment Promotion Committee:\nThe Committee was formed in compliance of guidelines issued by Reserve Bank of India to take decision on IT Strategies and to monitor the development in the area of IT Projects. IT Strategy Committee consists of Managing Director & CEO, Executive Directors, Government Nominee Director and three other Non-Executive Independent Directors. During the FY 2025-26. The Committee met 13 times on following dates:\n22-04-2025 19-05-2025 10-06-2025 10-07-2025 13-08-2025 20-09-2025 15-10-2025 17-11-2025 11-12-2025 20-12-2025 16-01-2026 16-02-2026 16-03-2026\nबैैंक ऑҰफ़ इंडिया / BANK OF INDIA वािर््षक रिपोर््ट / Annual Report 2025-26\n11. Directors Promotion Committee:","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c473","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":130,"text":"11. Directors Promotion Committee:\nThe Committee was formed on Ministry of Finance (DFS) Guidelines. The members of this Committee are Managing Director & CEO, GOI Nominee Director and RBI Nominee Director. During the FY 2025-26, it met 2 times on following dates:\n12-03-2026 13-03-2026\n12. Steering Committee of the Board on HR:\nThe Committee was formed to consider the HR related matters. The Members of this Committee are Managing Director & CEO, Executive Directors, Govt. Nominee Director, Shareholder Director and Non-Executive Independent Director. During the FY 2025-26 it met 12 times on following dates:\n30-05-2025 26-06-2025 28-07-2025 26-08-2025 26-09-2025 30-10-2025 28-11-2025 16-12-2025 30-12-2025 27-01-2026 27-02-2026 30-03-2026\n13. Committee for Monitoring High Value NPAs and Loss Assets:\nThe Committee was formed to monitor recovery & review of top 50 NPAs. This Committee consist of Non-Executive Chairman, Managing Director & CEO, Executive Directors, Govt. Nominee Director, General Manager – Recovery Department is the convener. During the FY 2025-26, it met 4 times on following dates:\n10.06.2025 26.08.2025 26.12.2025 09-03-2026\n14. Review Committee for Wilful Defaulters:\nThe Members of this Committee are Non-Executive Chairman, Managing Director & CEO, One Shareholder Directors During the FY 2025- 26, it met 4 times on following dates:","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c474","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":130,"text":"The Members of this Committee are Non-Executive Chairman, Managing Director & CEO, One Shareholder Directors During the FY 2025- 26, it met 4 times on following dates:\n30.05.2025 24.07.2025 26.12.2025 10-03-2026\n15. Independent Directors’ Committee:\nTwo Shareholder Directors and Non-Executive Chairman of the Bank are the members of this Committee. The independent Director’s Committee of the Board met once on 23-05-2025.\nDetails of attendance of the Independent Directors’ Committee for Meetings in FY 2025-26 are as follows:\nDirectors Name Meetings held during\nPeriod From To *V V.Shenoy 1 1 01-04-2025 28-11-2025 M R Kumar 1 1 01-04-2025 31-03-2026 Jamuna Ravi 1 1 01-04-2025 31-03-2026\nAttendance\ntheir tenure\nRecorded\n* V V Shenoy ceased to be member during the year\n16. Disciplinary Proceedings Committee:\nThe Members of this Committee are Managing Director & CEO, Govt. Nominee Director, RBI Nominee Director and one Shareholder Director. During the FY 2025-26, it met on 4 times on\n10-07-2025 25-08-2025 23-10-2025 10-03-2026\n17. Corporate Social Responsibility Committee:","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c475","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":130,"text":"17. Corporate Social Responsibility Committee:\nCorporate Social Responsibility Committee constituted in terms of Government of India – CSR – Voluntary Guidelines – 2009. Managing Director & CEO, four Executive Directors, two Independent Director and Non-Executive Chairman of the Bank are members of this Committee. The Committee met 4 times during the FY 2025-26 on following dates.\n17-07-2025 08.08.2025 17.12.2025 09-03-2026\n18. Committee for Performance Evaluation of Managing Director & Chief Executive Officer, Executive Director, Chief General Managers and General Managers:\nThis Committee is constituted as per Government of India, Ministry of Finance, Department of Financial Services Directives F. No. 9/5/2009- IR dated 30.08.2019. The Members of this Committee are Non-Executive Chairman, one Shareholder Directors, Govt. Nominee Director. The Committee met 3 times during FY 2025-26 on following dates :\n23-05-2025 29-07-2025 20.03.2026\nबैैंक ऑҰफ़ इंडिया / BANK OF INDIA वािर््षक रिपोर््ट / Annual Report 2025-26\n19. Group Governance Unit Committee:\nThe Committee consists of Chairman, Managing Director & CEO, four Executive Directors and Two Shareholder Directors. The Committee met 11 times during the Financial Year 2025-26 on the following dates.\n19-04-2025 23-05-2025 10-06-2025 10-07-2025 08-08-2025 06-09-2025 15-10-2025 18-11-2025 11-12-2025 16-02-2026 16-03-2026","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c476","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":131,"text":"19-04-2025 23-05-2025 10-06-2025 10-07-2025 08-08-2025 06-09-2025 15-10-2025 18-11-2025 11-12-2025 16-02-2026 16-03-2026\nDetails of Senior Management (Chief General Managers) as on 31st March 2026:\nSr. No. Name Date of Appointment Department 1 Shri Abhijit Bose 28-01-2022 General Operation, Premises 2 Shri Ashok Kumar Pathak 28-01-2022 Corporate Credit, Treasury, International, FBD 3 Shri Sudhiranjan Padhi 31-03-2023 Human Resources, Learning & Development, Finance, Planning, BPR, EASE 4 Shri P. K. Giri 31-03-2023 Compliance & GCCO 5 Shri P. Harikishan 01-04-2023 Risk Management 6 Shri Sharda Bhushan Rai 01-04-2023 Recovery & Credit Monitoring, Stressed Asset Recovery, Legal 7 Shri Nitin G. Deshpande 01-04-2023 Retail, Rural, MSME, Financial Inclusion, Digital Lending 8 Shri Rajesh S Ingle 06-11-2023 Inspection & Audit 9 Shri Prashant Thapliyal 01-03-2024 Resource Mobilisation, Publicity & PR, Marketing, Third Party Products & Government Business, CEBB, Call Centre 10 Shri Sunil Sharma 01-04-2025 FCGMO, Mumbai 11 Shri Raghvendra Kumar 29-09-2025 On Deputation CVO of Punjab National Bank 12 Shri Satyendra Singh 25-11-2025 Information Technology, Digital Banking, Digital Lending Dept., Data Analytics (DAD), IT (Governance & Excellence) & CTO 13 Shri Sankar Sen 01-01-2026 FCGMO, Pune\nShare Transfers and Redressal of Shareholders`/ Investors` Grievances:","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c477","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":131,"text":"Share Transfers and Redressal of Shareholders`/ Investors` Grievances:\na request to the depository participant for dematerialising the said securities.\nThe Bank has constituted the Share Transfer Committee of the Board to consider the transfer of shares and other related matters. In terms of SEBI guidelines dated 08-06-2018 and SEBI Press Release dated 03-12-2018, physical transfer of shares is not permitted after 31-03-2019. Thus, shareholders are requested to open a demat account and dematerialise their physical shareholding.\nThe RTA shall issue a reminder after the end of 45 days and 90 days from the date of issuance of Letter of Confirmation, informing the securities holder / claimant to submit the demat request.\nThe RTA shall retain the physical share certificate as per the existing procedure and deface the certificate with a stamp “Letter of Confirmation issued” on the face / reverse of the certificate, subsequent to processing the service request.\nFurther, in the interest of investors and with a view to enhance ease of dealing in securities markets by investors, SEBI, vide its circular dated 25-01-2022, decided that the listed entities shall henceforth issue the shares in dematerialised mode only while processing the following service requests:","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c478","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":131,"text":"Depository Participant shall generate the demat request on the basis of the Letter of Confirmation and forward the same to the Listed entity / RTA for processing the demat request.\nIf demat request is not received within 120 days of the Letter of Confirmation, shares shall be credited to the Suspense Escrow Demat Account of the entity.\n• Issue of duplicate securities certificate;\n• Claim from Unclaimed Suspense Account;\nIn compliance with SEBI (Listing Obligations & Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015, the Bank has appointed M/s Bigshare Services Pvt. Ltd., as its Registrar and Transfer Agent (RTA) with a mandate to process transfer of Shares, transmission, dividend, recording of shareholders’ requests, and solution of shareholders’ grievances amongst other activities connected with the issue of shares. For lodgement of any of these documents and for queries/complaints/grievances, shareholders and investors are requested to contact:\n• Renewal / Exchange of securities certificate;\n• Endorsement;\n• Sub-division / Splitting of securities certificate;\n• Consolidate of securities certificate / folios;\n• Transmission;\n• Transposition","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c479","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":131,"text":"• Transposition\nThe shareholder / claimant shall submit duly filled up Form ISR- 4 and the RTA / listed entity shall, after processing the service requests, issue a “Letter of Confirmation” instead of physical certificates to the shareholder / claimant within 30 days of such requests after removing objections, if any.\nFor Equity Shares and Debentures/ Bonds: Bigshare Services Pvt. Ltd., Unit: Bank of India, Office No S6-2, 6th Floor, Pinnacle Business Park, Next to Ahura Centre, Mahakali Caves Road, Andheri (East) Mumbai – 400093\nThe Letter of confirmation shall be valid for 120 days from the date of its issuance within which the shareholder / claimant shall make\nबैैंक ऑҰफ़ इंडिया / BANK OF INDIA वािर््षक रिपोर््ट / Annual Report 2025-26\nApart from the above, investors may also contact the Bank at its Investor Relations Cell at:\n2) SBI CAP Trustee Company Limited Mistry Bhavan 4th Floor, 122, Dinshaw Vaccha Road, Churchgate Mumbai – 400 020 Board No.022-4302 5500/5566 022-43025525 Email id : Corporate@sbicaptrustee.com\nStar House, 8th Floor, East Wing, C-5, G Block, Bandra-Kurla Complex, Bandra (E), Mumbai - 400 051, Phone: 022 – 6668 4490/4491, E-mail: headoffice.share@bankofindia.bank.in.\nAttendance of the Directors at the last Annual General Meeting:\nFor Privately placed Bonds, the Bank has appointed following Debenture Trustees:","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c480","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":132,"text":"For Privately placed Bonds, the Bank has appointed following Debenture Trustees:\nThe last Annual General Meeting i.e.29th Annual General Meeting of the Bank held on 27th June, 2025, in which following directors participated\n1) IDBI Trusteeship Services Ltd. Asian Building, Ground Floor, 17, R. Kamani Marg, Ballard Estate, Mumbai – 400 001. Ph.No. 022-4080 7000 Fax No. 022-6631 1776 Email id : itsl@idbitrustee.com\n1. Shri M. R. Kumar Chairman,\n2. Shri Rajneesh Karnatak, MD & CEO\n3. Shri Subrat Kumar, Executive Director\n4. Shri Rajiv Mishra, Executive Director\n5. Smt. Jamuna Ravi, Shareholder Director\n6. Shri Vishwanath V. Shenoy, (as on date ceased to shareholder director)\nLast 3 General Body Meetings held at Bank of India Head Office, Star House, Bandra Kuria Complex, Bandra (East), Mumbai - 400 051.\nNature of\nDate & Time Resolution\nSr. No.\nMeeting\n1) Approved Annual Financial results for the year 2024-25 2) Approved and declared dividend for the Financial Year 2024-25 3) Approved appointment of M/s. Sawant & Associates, as Secretarial Auditor of the Bank for a continuous period of five years\nFriday, 27th June 2025 at 11.00 am through Video Conferencing (VC)/ Other Audio Visual Means (OAVM)\n1. Twenty Ninth Annual General Meeting","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c481","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":132,"text":"1. Twenty Ninth Annual General Meeting\n1) Approved extension of term of Shri P R Rajagopal as Executive Director of the Bank. 2) Approved extension of term of Shri Subrat Kumar as Executive Director of the Bank.\nFriday, 7th November, 2025 at 1.00 P.M through Video Conference (VC)/ Other Audio Visual Means (OAVC).\n2. Extraordinary General Meeting\n1) Approved Annual Financial results for the year 2023-24 2) Approved and declared dividend for the Financial Year 2023-24 3) Approved extension of term of Shri P R Rajagopal as Executive Director of the Bank.\nTuesday, 25th June 2024 at 11.00 am through Video Conferencing (VC)/ Other Audio Visual Means (OAVM)\n3. Twenty Eighth Annual General Meeting\n4) Approved extension of term of Shri M. Karthikeyan as Executive Director of the Bank. 5) Approved appointment of Shri Ashok Narain as Non- Executive Nominee Director of the Bank 6) Approved appointment of Shri Rajiv Mishra as Executive Director of the Bank 7) Approved appointment of Shri M.R. Kumar as part-time Non-Official Director as well as Non-Executive Chairman of the Bank.\n1) Election of One Director from amongst the Shareholders of the Bank other than the Central Government. 2) Appointment of Shri Manoj M.Ayyappan as Govt. Nominee Director of the Bank.\nTuesday, 3rd December, 2024 at 11.00 A.M through Video Conference (VC)/Other Audio Visual Means (OAVC).","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c482","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":132,"text":"Tuesday, 3rd December, 2024 at 11.00 A.M through Video Conference (VC)/Other Audio Visual Means (OAVC).\n4. Extraordinary General Meeting\n1) Approved Annual Financial results for the year 2022-23 2) Approved and declared dividend for the Financial Year 2022-23 3) Appointment of Shri Bhushan Kumar Sinha as Non-Executive Nominee Director of the Bank. 4) Appointment of Shri Subrat Kumar as Executive Director of the Bank.\nTuesday, 27th June 2023 at 11.00 am through Video Conferencing (VC)/ Other Audio Visual Means (OAVM)\n5. Twenty Seventh Annual General Meeting\nबैैंक ऑҰफ़ इंडिया / BANK OF INDIA वािर््षक रिपोर््ट / Annual Report 2025-26\n5) Appointment of Shri Rajneesh Karnatak as the Managing Director & Chief Executive Officer of the Bank. 6) Appointment of Shri Munish Kumar Ralhan as part-time Non-Official Director of the Bank. 7) Raising of capital by way of issuing fresh equity shares and or by way of issuance of Tier I & Tier II Capital as per BASEL III guidelines.\nDisclosures:\nThe sitting fees paid to the Directors for attending/chairing the Board and its sub-committee Meetings w.e.f. 28-10-2025 is as below. Please also note that the existing ceiling of Rs. 25 lakhs has been removed w. e. f. 28.10.2025","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c483","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":133,"text":"The sitting fees paid to the Directors for attending/chairing the Board and its sub-committee Meetings w.e.f. 28-10-2025 is as below. Please also note that the existing ceiling of Rs. 25 lakhs has been removed w. e. f. 28.10.2025\nThe Bank is governed by the Banking Regulations Act, 1949, Banking Companies (Acquisition and Transfer of Undertakings) Act 1970 and Nationalised Banks (Management & Miscellaneous Provisions) Scheme 1970 and is regulated by Reserve Bank of India. Bank has complied with the provisions of SEBI (LODR) Regulations, 2015 except where the provisions of these regulations are not in conformity with the Nationalisation Act and the guidelines issued by RBI and Government of India.\nMeeting Amount per meeting\nSr. No.\nRs.90,000\n(a) For attending Board meeting\nRs.45,000\n(b) For attending meeting of Board committee\ni) Remuneration of Directors:\nThe Managing Director & CEO and Executive Directors (whole time directors) are paid remuneration by way of salary as per rules framed by the Government of India. At present the Bank has no Stock Option Scheme. Details of remuneration paid to the Managing Director & CEO and Executive Directors are given below:\nRs.10,000/- (in addition to above)\n(c) For chairing Board meeting\nRs.5,000/- (in addition to above)\n(d) For chairing meeting of Board committee","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c484","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":133,"text":"(d) For chairing meeting of Board committee\nIn addition to sitting fees, every such director travelling in connection with the work of the Bank shall be reimbursed Travelling & Halting expenses, if any, in terms of the provisions of clauses 17 of the Nationalised Banks (Management and Miscellaneous Provisions) Scheme, 1970, on such basis as may be fixed by Central Government from time to time.\nName Designation 2025-26 2024-25\nSr. No.\n62,94,742 52,69,865\n1. Shri Rajneesh Karnatak\nManaging Director & CEO\n68,16,348 59,42,538\n2. Shri P R Rajagopal\nExecutive Director\nii) Disclosure of Material Transactions and Pecuniary Relationship:\n18,68,640 49,17,186\n3. Shri M. Karthikeyan\nExecutive Director (Super annuated on 31st March, 2025)\nOther than those in the normal course of banking business, the Bank has not entered into any materially significant transaction with its promoters, directors or the management, their subsidiaries or relatives etc., which may have potential conflict with the interests of the Bank at large. There was no pecuniary relationship or transactions of the Non-Executive Director vis-a-vis the bank during the year.\n76,93,522 51,40,710\n4. Shri Subrat Kumar\nExecutive Director\n72,54,345 35,65,716\n5. Shri Rajiv Mishra\nExecutive Director\n6. Shri Pramod Kumar Dwibedi *\n16,36,274 -\nExecutive Director","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c485","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":133,"text":"Executive Director\nIt is an established practice in the Bank that Directors do not take part in the deliberations of the Board and other Sub- Committees of the Board, when matters relating to them or to their relatives are discussed.\n* Shri Pramod Kumar Dwibedi Executive Director w.e.f. 24.11.2025\nThe Sitting Fee is paid to the non-Executive Directors as per the provisions of Nationalized Banks (Management & Miscellaneous Provisions) Scheme 1970, read with Government guidelines for attending Board and Board Committee meetings. Details of sitting fee paid during the Year 2025-26 are as under (No sitting fee is payable to Whole Time Directors and Directors representing Government of India):\niii) Proceeds from Public issues, Right issues, Preferential issues, Tier 2 bonds, Infra Bonds etc.\nDuring the year under review, the Bank has raised the following funds:\nParticulars (Investors) Number\nIssue\nSr. No.\nDate of Allotment\nSize\nof Shares/\nSr. No.\nName Designation Sitting Fees Paid\nIn Crore 1. 12.12.2025 Unsecured, Subordinate Non-Convertible, Taxable, fully paid-up, Redeemable Basel III compliant 7.28 % Tier II Bonds, Series XVIII in the nature of debentures of face value Rs.1Crore each (the \"Bonds\")\nBonds\n(in Rs.) 1. *Shri V V Shenoy Shareholder Director 30,90,000 2. Shri Ashok Narain RBI Nominee Director 36,05,000\n2,500 2,500","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c486","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":133,"text":"2,500 2,500\n3. Shri M R Kumar Chairman 42,45,000 4. Smt.Jamuna Ravi Shareholder Director 48,00,000 5. Shri Prabodh Parikh Shareholder Director 26,00,000\n* Shri V V Shenoy ceased to be member of the Board w.e.f.29.11.2025\nबैैंक ऑҰफ़ इंडिया / BANK OF INDIA वािर््षक रिपोर््ट / Annual Report 2025-26\nTraining details\nSr. No.\nName of Non-Executive Director\nParticulars (Investors) Number\nSr. No.\nDate of Allotment\nIssue\nof Shares/\nSize\n4. Shri Ashok Narain Certification Programme for IT & Cyber Security for Board Members\nIn Crore 2. 26.12.2025 Bank has raised Long Term Infra Bonds of Rs.10,000 Crore through Long Term Infra Bond Series IV at 7.23%. Face Value of the bond is Rs.1,00,000/-\nBonds\n10,00,000 10,000\nxi) Code of Conduct for Directors and Senior Management is posted on Bank’s website – https://bankofindia. bank.in/documents/20121/442930/BOI_Code_of_ Conduct_Dir_19042021.pdf/c54b5953-f8df-6d80-0b31- 19b3bc4d3cdc?t=1663586179347\nxii) Whistle Blower Policy is posted at Bank’s website – https:// bankofindia.bank.in/documents/20121/25744421/2-Whistle- Blower-Policy-2024.pdf.","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c487","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":134,"text":"xii) Whistle Blower Policy is posted at Bank’s website – https:// bankofindia.bank.in/documents/20121/25744421/2-Whistle- Blower-Policy-2024.pdf.\niv) The capital funds of Rs. 2,500 Crore were raised with the primary objective of augmenting Tier-II Capital for Strengthening Capital Adequacy Ratio and for improving the long - term resources of the Bank and the same were utilised for the said purpose. Infrastructure Bonds of Rs. 10,000 Crore was raised for funding long term project in infrastructure sub sectors and affordable housing as prescribed by Reserve Bank of India and the same were utilised for the said purpose.\nxiii) Related Party Policy transaction – The Related party transactions are reported to Audit Committee. The Bank’s policy on Related Party transaction is posted on Bank’s website– https://bankofindia.bank.in/ documents/20121/25744421/2-Whistle-Blower-Policy-2024. pdf.\nDetails of related party transactions are as detailed under AS-18.","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c488","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":134,"text":"Details of related party transactions are as detailed under AS-18.\nv) In terms of SEBI’s circular No. D&CC/FITTC/CIR-16 dated December 31, 2002 a Reconciliation of Share Capital Audit is conducted on a quarterly basis by a firm of practising company secretaries, for the purpose of, inter alia, reconciliation of the total admitted equity share capital with the depositories and in the physical form with the total issued/paid up equity capital of Bank of India. Certificate issued in this regard is placed before the Board of Directors and forwarded to BSE and NSE, where the equity shares of Bank of India are listed.\nxiv) Remuneration Policy - The Remuneration of the Managing Director & CEO, Executive Directors is fixed by the Government of India. Salary of other staff members is as per the Tripartite Agreement of the IBA.\nxv) Takeover Code: The Bank has also complied, from time to time, with the provisions of SEBI (Substantial Acquisition of Shares and Takeovers) Regulations, 2011 as amended.\nvi) There are no strictures / penalties imposed on the Bank by SEBI / Stock Exchanges during the last three years except as disclosed in the Corporate Governance Report for March, 2025.\nxvi) Compliance with SEBI (Prohibition of Insider Trading) Regulations, 2015:","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c489","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":134,"text":"xvi) Compliance with SEBI (Prohibition of Insider Trading) Regulations, 2015:\nIn pursuance of the Regulations, the Bank has formulated Code of conduct for Prevention of Insider Trading for Designated Employees and Directors for dealing in securities of the Bank. Various forms have been designed to receive periodical information from the Designated Employees and the Directors of the Bank, as required in terms of these Regulations. Further, the Trading Window for dealing in shares of the Bank was kept closed for the Directors and Designated Employees of the Bank as per the following details:\nvii) Disclosure of commodity price risk and commodity hedging activities – Not Applicable\nviii) At present, the Bank does not have any material subsidiary.\nix) Independent Directors Meeting: The separate meeting of Independent Directors was held on 23.05.2025.\nx) Training of Non-Executive Directors:\nFollowing training was imparted to Non-Executive Directors\nPurpose of closure\nDates of closure of trading window\nTraining details\nSr. No.\nName of Non-Executive Director\nw.e.f Wednesday, 01.07.2025 To Friday 29.07.2025\nDeclaration of Financial Results for the Quarter ended 30th June, 2025. w.e.f Wednesday, 01.10.2025 To Sunday 19.10.2025","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c490","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":134,"text":"Declaration of Financial Results for the Quarter ended 30th June, 2025. w.e.f Wednesday, 01.10.2025 To Sunday 19.10.2025\n1. Shri M. R. Kumar Certification Programme for IT & Cyber Security for Board Members 2. Smt. Jamuna Ravi Certification Programme for IT & Cyber Security for Board Members 3. Shri Prabodh Parikh Certification Programme for IT & Cyber Security for Board Members\nDeclaration of Financial Results for the Quarter ended 30th September, 2025. w.e.f Thursday, 01.01.2026 To Friday 23.01.2026\nDeclaration of Financial Results for the Quarter ended 31st December, 2025. w.e.f Wednesday, 01.04.2026 To Sunday 11.05.2026\nDeclaration of Financial Results for the year ended 31st March, 2026.\nबैैंक ऑҰफ़ इंडिया / BANK OF INDIA वािर््षक रिपोर््ट / Annual Report 2025-26\nListing on Stock Exchanges\nxvii) Details of fees paid to Auditors:\nThe shares of the Bank are listed on The BSE Ltd., and The National Stock Exchange of India Limited. The stock scrip codes are as follows:\nSr. No.\nParticulars Amount (Rs. In Crore) 1 Amount paid to Auditors of the Bank for the year 2025-26\n86.46\nThe BSE Ltd. (BSE) 532149 National Stock Exchange of India Limited (NSE)\n89.31\n2 Amount paid to Auditors of the Bank and its subsidiaries for the year 2025-26\nBANKINDIA\nxviii) Disclosure in relation to the Sexual Harassment of Women\nISIN Number INE084A01016","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c491","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":135,"text":"ISIN Number INE084A01016\nat workplace (Prevention, Prohibition and Redressal) Act, 2013.\nAnnual listing fee for 2025-26 has been paid to both the Stock Exchanges.\nNo of Complaints Filed during the FY 2025-26 6 Complaints resolved during the year FY 2025-26 6 Complaints Pending for Resolution FY 2025-26 0\nThe high & low of the share price of the Company during the year 2025-26 on NSE is as follows:\nPeriod Highest Rs. Lowest Rs. Volume of Share Traded April-2025 121.65 103.00 20,74,21,753 May-2025 122.61 104.20 25,36,90,530 June -2025 130.24 111.56 26,01,35,395 July-2025 121.63 110.30 18,65,60,751 Aug-2025 117.31 108.81 8,63,52,775 Sep-2025 123.87 110.68 15,06,94,409 Oct-2025 142.71 122.20 27,59,35,728 Nov-2025 151.43 138.55 17,38,36,328 Dec-2025 149.40 136.71 15,11,82,114 Jan-2026 169.90 142.90 29,92,19,527 Feb -2026 178.36 146.40 23,73,96,614 March-2026 174.40 136.20 18,06,32,390 The Bank has issued Basel III Compliant Non-Convertible Bonds in the nature of Debentures (Additional Tier I, Tier II capital) and Infra Bonds from time to time. The relevant details thereof are as under:\nDetails of Material Subsidiaries of the Bank: None of the Subsidiaries of the Bank is a Material Subsidiary.\nMeans of Communication:","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c492","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":135,"text":"Means of Communication:\nThe quarterly and half-yearly financial results (unaudited but subject to limited review by the Statutory Auditors) and audited Annual results were published in the newspapers - Business Standard in English, Business Standard in Hindi and Loksatta in Marathi (Regional language). The results were also displayed on the Bank’s website at www.bankofindia.bank.in. The presentations made to Institutional Investors are also available on Bank’s website.\nAs required by SEBI LODR Regulations, Bank of India files its financial and other information online on the web portals of the Stock Exchanges.\nFinancial Calendar: From 1st April, 2026:\n08.05.2026\nBoard Meeting for considering Annual Audited Accounts of Bank of India and recommendation of dividend, if any\nBANK OF INDIA – TIER I, TIER II AND LONG TERM INFRA BONDS POSITION AS ON 31.03.2026\nCoupon\nISIN No.\nParticulars of the Issue\nTotal Value (Rs. in Crores)\nPosting of Annual Report By Email /Speed Post/Courier.\nRate\n08.06.2026\nLast date for receipt of Authorised Representation","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c493","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":135,"text":"Last date for receipt of Authorised Representation\nAdditional Tier I Series VIII 8.57% 1500 INE084A08169 Tier II Bonds Series XV 7.14% 1,800 INE084A08151 Series XVI 7.88% 2,000 INE084A08177 Series XVII 7.49% 2,500 INE084A08193 Series XVIII 7.28% 2,500 INE084A08227 Long Term Infra Bonds Series I 7.54% 5,000 INE084A08185 Series II 7.41% 5,000 INE084A08201 Series III 7.50% 2,690 INE084A08219 Series IV 7.23% 10,000 INE084A08235 TOTAL 32,990\n29.05.2026\nRecord Date for payment of dividend\nDate, Time, Venue of 30th AGM 15.06.2026 At Bank of India,\nHead Office, Star House, Bandra Kurla Complex, Bandra (East), Mumbai – 400 051 through Video Conferencing (VC/Other Audio Visual Means(OAVM)\nWithin 45 days of the relevant quarter.\nBoard Meeting for considering Un-audited result for first 3 quarters\nAll these bonds are listed on National Stock Exchange of India Ltd. and the Bank has paid the Annual listing fee for 2025-26 to the Stock Exchange.\nबैैंक ऑҰफ़ इंडिया / BANK OF INDIA वािर््षक रिपोर््ट / Annual Report 2025-26\nSummary of Credit Ratings Bank of India FY2025-26:\nPAYMENT OF DIVIDEND / RECORD DATE:","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c494","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":136,"text":"PAYMENT OF DIVIDEND / RECORD DATE:\nThe Board of Directors of the Bank has recommended a dividend of Rs. 4.65 per equity share (i.e. 46.50%) of face value of Rs.10/- each to the Shareholders for the year 2025-26, subject to the approval of the Shareholders at the AGM. It has been decided to pay the dividend to the Shareholders whose names appear on the Register of Shareholders / Beneficial owners as furnished by NSDL / CDSL as on, 29.05.2026 (hereinafter referred to as Record Date). The dividend will be paid to the shareholders within 30 days from the date of declaration at the Annual General Meeting (15.06.2026, Monday).\nRating Agency Instrument Present\nRating Action\nRating\nCRISIL Limited Basel III Tier I\nAA (Stable) Reaffirmed\nBonds\nBasel III Tier II\nAA+ (Stable) Reaffirmed\nBonds\nAA+ (Stable) Reaffirmed\nLong Term Infra Bonds\nIndia Ratings Basel III Tier II\nAA+ (Stable) Reaffirmed\nBonds\nUNCLAIMED DIVIDEND, IF ANY:\nAA+ (Stable) Reaffirmed\nLong Term Infra Bonds\nThe shareholders who have not encashed their Dividend Warrants / received dividend for the year 2021-22, 2022-23, 2023-24 and 2024-25 are requested to contact the Registrar and Transfer Agent (RTA) of the Bank, M/s Bigshare Services Pvt. Ltd., for receiving the dividend.\nBasel III Tier II\nAA+ (Stable) Reaffirmed\nCare Ratings Ltd.\nBonds\nAA+ (Stable) Reaffirmed\nLong Term Infra Bonds","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c495","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":136,"text":"Long Term Infra Bonds\nAs per Section 10B of the Nationalisation Act, the amount of dividend remaining unpaid or unclaimed for a period of seven years is required to be transferred to the Investor Education and Protection Fund (IEPF) established by the Central Govt. under section 125 of the Companies Act, 2013. All the dividends unclaimed for a period of seven years (pertaining to FY upto 2014-15) have been transferred to the IEPF Authority. Bank has not declared any dividend during FY 2015-16 to FY 2020-21.\nCertificate of\nA1+ Assigned\nDeposit\nInfomeric Valuation & Rating\nBasel III Tier I\nAAA (Stable) Reaffirmed\nBonds\nAcuite Ratings Basel III Tier I\nAA+ (Stable) Reaffirmed\nBonds\nBasel III Tier II\nAAA (Stable) Reaffirmed\nBonds\nUNCLAIMED SHARES:\nICRA Basel III Tier II\nAA+ (Stable) Assigned\nAll shares in respect of which dividend declared up to FY 2014- 15 has remained unpaid/unclaimed for seven consecutive years or more and in respect of which no valid claim was received on or before 07 March 2026, have been transferred by the Bank to IEPF.\nBonds\nFitch Ratings (International Rating)\nCorporate Rating (Long/\nBBB- (Stable) Reaffirmed\nShort)","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c496","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":136,"text":"Short)\nPrior to transfer, individual communication was sent on 08.12.2025 to the concerned shareholders at their registered addresses/e- mail ID as per records available with the Bank/RTA/Depositories. The Bank had also published notice on 08.12.2025 in newspapers requesting shareholders to lodge their claims by 07 March 2026.\nDIVIDEND / INTEREST PAYMENT THROUGH ELECTRONIC MODES\nThe Bank is paying Dividend on Shares / Interest on Bonds to the Investors through various electronic modes, wherever mandate is given by the Investors. For this purpose, Bank is using the services of National Automated Clearing House (NACH), National Electronic Clearing Services (NECS), RTGS, NEFT and Direct Credit, etc.\nThe details of such shareholders and shares transferred to IEPF are available on the Bank’s website: www.bankofindia.bank.in.\nInvestors may lodge their mandate with Bank’s Registrar and Transfer Agent, M/s Bigshare Services Pvt. Ltd., at the address given in this report.\nStatus of shares lying in Suspense Escrow Account:\nOpening Balance as on\nClosing Balance as on\n01.04.2025 Addition during the\nNo. of request recd. & Shares Debited during the FY 2025-26\nFY 2025-26\n31.03.2026\nNo. of Shareholders\nNo. of Shares\nNo. of Shareholders\nNo. of Shares\nNo. of Shareholders\nNo. of Shares\nNo. of Shareholders\nNo. of Shares\n12 1700 10 2100 4 600 18 3200","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c497","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":136,"text":"12 1700 10 2100 4 600 18 3200\nThe voting rights on these shares shall remain frozen till the rightful owner of such shares claims the shares.\nबैैंक ऑҰफ़ इंडिया / BANK OF INDIA वािर््षक रिपोर््ट / Annual Report 2025-26\nShareholding Pattern as on 31.03.2026:\nNumber of Shares % of Holding Shares under\nCategory of Shareholders Number of Shareholders\n% of Shares under Lock-in\nLock- in\nPromoter(Government of India) 1 3,34,08,61,720 73.38 0 0.00\nMutual Funds 32 15,52,70,254 3.41 0 0.00\nAlternate Investment Funds 11 20,77,958 0.05 0 0.00\nFinancial Institution/Bank 13 8,691 0.00 0 0.00\nInsurance Company 22 46,75,71,536 10.27 0 0.00\nQualified Institutional Investors 1 1,06,02,943 0.23 0 0.00\nBodies Corporate 1,466 2,10,62,757 0.46 0 0.00\nForeign Financial Institution Investor 329 33,06,71,756 7.26 0 0.00\nIndian public 6,17,121 21,38,16,144 4.70 0 0.00\nOthers 7,193 107,24,107 0.24 0 0.00\nTotal 6,26,189 4,55,26,67,866 100.00 0 0.00\nShareholding of persons (Public) holding more than 1% of the total number of shares:\nName of the Shareholder Number of Shares % of Holding LIC of India 36,88,28,543 8.10\nDistribution of Shareholdings as on 31st March, 2026:\nFolio Shares\nNo. of Equity Shares held\nNos. % age Nos. % age\nUpto 500 5,74,622 90.09 567,65,170 1.25\n501 to 1000 31,231 4.90 243,91,620 0.54\n1001 to 5000 26,785 4.20 576,69,973 1.27\n5001 to 10000 2,786 0.44 203,00,647 0.44","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c498","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":137,"text":"5001 to 10000 2,786 0.44 203,00,647 0.44\n10001 & Above 2,359 0.37 43,935,40,456 96.50\nTotal 6,37,783 100.00 4,55,26,67,866 100.00\nDematerialisation of Shares:\nThe Bank’s shares are being traded compulsorily in Demat form only. The Bank has entered into agreements with both the Depositories viz. National Securities Depositories Ltd. (NSDL) and Central Depository Services (India) Ltd. (CDSL) for dematerialization of shares.\nParticulars of shares in Demat and Physical form held by the shareholders as of 31.03.2026 are as under:\nNo. of Shareholders Shareholders in % No. of Shares Shareholding %\nNSDL 1,84,629 28.95 106,95,40,552 23.49 CDSL 3,68,038 57.71 347,06,02,460 76.23 Physical 85,116 13.35 1,25,24,854 0.28 Total 6,37,783 100.00 455,26,67,866 100.00\nOther Compliances:\n1. The certificate issued by the practicing Company Secretary, regarding compliance of mandatory stipulations of Corporate Governance in terms of the listing agreement with the Stock Exchange is attached.\n2. A Certificate from a Company Secretary in practice that none of the Directors on the Board of the Bank have been debarred or disqualified from being appointed or continuing as Directors of companies by the Board / Ministry of Corporate Affairs or any such statutory authority, is enclosed.","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c499","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":137,"text":"2. A Certificate from a Company Secretary in practice that none of the Directors on the Board of the Bank have been debarred or disqualified from being appointed or continuing as Directors of companies by the Board / Ministry of Corporate Affairs or any such statutory authority, is enclosed.\n3. Secretarial Audit Report: In Compliance of Regulation 24A of SEBI LODR 2015, the Annual Secretarial Compliance Report (Form MR 3) is enclosed.\n4. Financial Statements of Subsidiaries: In compliance of Regulation 46(2) of SEBI LODR 2015, the Audited Financial Statements of subsidiaries have been uploaded on our website i.e. www.bankofindia.bank.in.\nबैैंक ऑҰफ़ इंडिया / BANK OF INDIA वािर््षक रिपोर््ट / Annual Report 2025-26\nCompliance of Mandatory / Non Mandatory Requirements:\nThe Bank has complied with the following Discretionary Requirement as mentioned under Part –E of Schedule II of SEBI Listing Regulations, 2015:\nNon Mandatory requirements Status of implementation\nSr. No.\n1. The Board – A Non-Executive Chairman may be entitled to maintain a Chairman’s office at the company’s expenses\nThe Chairman’s Position is Non- Executive and there is a separate office in the Bank.\n2. Shareholder’s Rights- A half-yearly declaration of financial performance including summary of the significant events in last six- months, may be sent to shareholders.","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c500","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":138,"text":"2. Shareholder’s Rights- A half-yearly declaration of financial performance including summary of the significant events in last six- months, may be sent to shareholders.\nThe quarterly/year to date/ Annual Financial Results are sent to NSE & BSE & published in Newspapers and placed on Bank’s website including highlights. Quarterly results, press release and analyst presentation is sent to all shareholders by email.\n3. Modified Opinion (s) in Audit Report –The listed entity may move towards a regime of financial statements with unmodified audit opinion.\nThe Bank’s Annual Financial Statements are with unmodified audit opinion.\n4. Reporting of Internal Auditor All internal auditors are appointed by our Inspection and Audit Department, which reports to Audit Committee.\nThe Bank is having this position. GOI has appointed Non- Executive Chairman Shri M.R. Kumar.\n5. Separate posts of Chairperson and Chief Executive Officer- The listed entity may appoint separate persons to the post of Chairperson and Managing Director or Chief Executive Officer.\nCompliance status of corporate governance requirements:\nBank is in compliance with corporate governance requirements specified in regulation 17 to 27 and clauses (b) to (i) of sub regulation 46 of SEBI (LODR) Regulations, 2015 except following:\n(a) Board Composition (Regulation 17(1)): Bank has Chairperson who is non-executive director.","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c501","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":138,"text":"(a) Board Composition (Regulation 17(1)): Bank has Chairperson who is non-executive director.\nBoard Composition - Till 23.11.2025, our Bank has complied with Board composition requirements. Upon appointment of Executive Director Shri Pramod Kumar Dwibedi on 24.11.2025, the number of Directors on Bank’s Board has increased to 10, out of which 3 Directors are independent. Hence from 24.11.2025, 1/3rd of the Board composition is not independent. As the Central Government was in the process of nominating other Directors of the Bank and the vacancies have not been filled in, the Bank was not in a position to comply with the referred regulations. Due to above reasons, one third of the Board was not independent from 24.11.2025.\n(b) Audit Committee Composition (Regulation 18): Our Bank is a corresponding new bank constituted under the Banking Companies (Acquisition and Transfer of Undertakings) Act, 1970 (the Act). Composition of the Board of Directors of the Bank is governed by this Act.\nThe Central Government appoints Whole time Directors including the Managing Director and is entitled to nominate Non- Executive Directors identified and selected from various defined categories under the Act who can be considered as Independent Directors.","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c502","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":138,"text":"The Central Government appoints Whole time Directors including the Managing Director and is entitled to nominate Non- Executive Directors identified and selected from various defined categories under the Act who can be considered as Independent Directors.\nShareholders other than the Central Government are entitled to elect up to 3 Directors depending on the percentage of non- governmental shareholding in the Bank.\nAt present, Bank is having two Shareholder’s Directors who are considered as Independent Directors. One Non-Official Director appointed by Government of India is also considered as Independent Director.\nPresently, Audit Committee of the Board (ACB) is constituted as per the Circulars issued by RBI from time to time.\nAs per DFS guidelines no. 16/11/2015-BO.I dated 17.06.2016, any director who is on the Management Committee / Credit Approval Committee shall not be on the Audit committee in any capacity. As per the RBI guidelines, the Chairperson of the Board cannot be a member of the Audit Committee.\nOne Independent Director, Mr. Prabodh Parikh, is member of Management Committee and other Committees and thus cannot be part of the ACB.\nShri M R Kumar is Non-Executive Chairman and Independent Director and he cannot be a member of the ACB as per RBI guidelines.\nHence, the Bank is not in a position to have two third of the independent members on ACB.","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c503","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":138,"text":"Hence, the Bank is not in a position to have two third of the independent members on ACB.\nThe Bank has already taken up this matter with Department of Financial Services, Ministry of Finance, Government of India for immediate filling up of various vacancies at the Board level. Once these vacancies are filled up by the Government of India, our Bank will be able to comply with the requirements of Audit Committee composition.\nबैैंक ऑҰफ़ इंडिया / BANK OF INDIA वािर््षक रिपोर््ट / Annual Report 2025-26\nSAWANT & ASSOCIATES\nसाववंत एंड एसोसिएट्स\nPRACTISING COMPANY SECRETARY\nप्रैक््टटिस करने वाले कंपनी सचिव\nकॉॉұ र्पोोरेेट प्रशाासन पर प्रमाणपत्र\nCERTIFICATE ON CORPORATE GOVERNANCE\nThe Members, Bank of India, Star House, C-5, `G’ Block, Bandra-Kurla Complex, Bandra (East), Mumbai 400 051\nसदस्यगण, बैंंक ऑҰफ़ इंंडिɇया स्टाार हााऊस, सी-5, ‘जीी’ ब्लाॅॅҰक, बांं�द्राा-कुुर्लाӇ काॅॅұ म्पलेेक्स, बांं�द्राा (पूूर्वव), मुंं�बई – 400 051.\nWe have examined all the relevant records of the Bank of India (“the Bank/Company”) for the purpose of certifying compliance with the conditions of the Corporate Governance under Regulation 17 to 27, 46 and Schedule V of the SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulation, 2015 entered into with National Stock Exchange of India Limited and BSE Limited (Stock Exchanges) for the financial year from April 01, 2025 to March 31, 2026.","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c504","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":139,"text":"हमनेे 01 अप्रैैल, 2025 सेे 31 मार्चच, 2026 तक केे विƼत्‍‍तीय वर्षष केे लि�ए नेेशनल स्टाॅॅǛक एक्सचेंंज ऑǛफ़ इंंडििƧया लि�मि�टेेड और बीीएसई लि�मि�टेेड (स्टाॅॅǛक एक्सचेंंज) केे साथƫ हुए सूूचीीकरण करार केे तहत कॉॉΖर्पोोरेेट प्रशाासन प्रणााली की शर्तोंं, जि�नकाा उल्लेेख सेेबीी (सूूचीीबद्धता बाध्̒ यताएंं एवंं प्रकटीकरण आवश्यकताएंं) विƼनि�यम, 2015 केे विƼनि�यम 17 सेे 27, 46 एवंं अनुुसूूचीी V केे प्रावधाƭानोंं� मेंं कि�या गया हैै, केे अनुुपाालन केे प्रमााणीकरण केे प्रयोो जन सेे बैंंक ऑǛफ़ इंंडििƧया (‘’दीी बैंंक/कंंपनीी’’) केे सभीी संंगत अभि�लेेखोंं� की जांं�चच की हैै।\nThe compliance with conditions of Corporate Governance is the responsibility of the Management. Our examination was limited to procedures and implementation processes adopted by the bank to ensure compliance with the conditions of Corporate Governance. This Certificate is neither an audit nor an expression of opinion on the Financial Statements of the Company.\nकॉॉΖर्पोोरेेट प्रशाासन की शर्तोंं का अनुुपाालन प्रबंंधन की जि�म्मेेदारी हैै। हमारी जांं�चच कॉॉΖर्पोोरेेट प्रशाासन प्रणााली की शर्तोंं का अनुुपाालन कोो सुुनि�श्चिि͵˨त करनेे केे लि�ए बैंंक द्वाारा अपनााई गई कार्ययप्रणाली तथाƫा उसकेे कार्याा�न्वयन तक सीमि�त थी। यह प्रमााणपत्र न कोोई लेेखा परीीक्षाșा हैै और न कंंपनीी केे विƼत्तीीय विƼवरणोंं� पर हमारी राय की कोोई अभि�व्यक्ति́ ि हैै।","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c505","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":139,"text":"In our opinion and to the best of our information and according to the explanations and information furnished to us, we certify that the Bank has complied with all the conditions of Corporate Governance as stipulated in the SEBI (LODR) 2015.\nहमारी राय मेंं और हमेंं प्राप्‍‍त जानकाारी केे अनुुसार और हमेंं दि�ए गए स्पष्टीीकरण केे अनुुसार हम प्रमााणि�त करतेे हैंं कि� बैंंक नेे ऊपर उल्लेेख कि�ए गए सेेबीी (एलओडीआर) 2015 मेंं नि�र्धाƭा�रि�त कॉॉΖर्पोोरेेट प्रशाासन प्रणााली की शर्तोंं कोो पूूरा कि�या हैै।\nUDIN: A041210H000267194\nFor Sawant & Associates Practising Company Secretary\nयूूडीआईएन : A041210H000267194\nकृृतेे सावंंत एंंड एसोसि�एट््स प्रैैक्टि́ िस करनेे वालेे कंंपनीी सचि�व\nPrachi Prakash Sawant Membership No.: A41210 COP No.: 16317 PR: 2615/2022\nप्रााचीी प्रकााश साावंंत सदस्य संं: A41210 सीओपीी नंं: 16317 पीीआर: 2615/2022\nPlace: Mumbai Date: 04/05/2026\nस्थान: मुंं�बई दि�नांं�क : 04/05/2026\nबैैंक ऑҰफ़ इंडिया / BANK OF INDIA वािर््षक रिपोर््ट / Annual Report 2025-26\nSAWANT & ASSOCIATES\nसाववंत एंड एसोसिएट्स\nPRACTISING COMPANY SECRETARY\nप्रैक््टटिस करने वाले कंपनी सचिव\nनि�देेशकोंं� की गैैर-अयोग्यता का प्रमाणपत्र\nCERTIFICATE OF NON-DISQUALIFICATION OF DIRECTORS\n[सेेबीी (सूूचीीबद्धता बाध्‍̒ ‍यताएंं एवंं प्रकटीकरण अपेेक्षााएंं) विƼनि�यम, 2015 केे\n(Pursuant to Regulation 34(3) and Schedule V Para Clause (10) (i) of the SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements)","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c506","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":140,"text":"(Pursuant to Regulation 34(3) and Schedule V Para Clause (10) (i) of the SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements)\nविƼनि�यम 34(3) तथाƫा अनुुसूूचीी V, पैैरा सी, खण्ड (10)(i) केे अनुुसार]\nRegulations, 2015)\nप्रति� ,\nTo,\nबैंंक ऑǛफ़ इंंडििƧया केे सदस्‍‍य\nThe Members of Bank of India.\nहमनेे बैंंक ऑǛफ़ इंंडििƧया, जि�सकाा प्रधाƭान कार्याा�लय, सी-5, जी ब्‍‍लॉॉǛक, बांं�द्राा- कुुर्लाा� कॉॉΖम्प्लेेक्स, बांं�द्राा (पूूर्वव), मुंं�बई – 400 051 (इसकेे बाद इसेे “बैंंक” कहा जाएगा), हैै, केे नि�देेशकोंं� सेे प्राप्‍‍त प्रासंंगि�क रजि�स्‍टरोंं�, रि�कॉॉΖर्डड, फॉॉΖर्मम, रि�टर्नन तथाƫा प्रकटनोंं� की जांं�चच की हैै, जि�न्‍हेंं भारतीय प्रति�भूू ति� एवंं विƼनि�मय बोोर्डड (सूूचीीबद्धता बाध्‍̒ ‍यताएंं एवंं प्रकटीकरण अपेेक्षााएंं) विƼनि�यमन, 2015 केे विƼनि�यम 34(3) केे साथƫ पठिƦत अनुुसूूचीी V पैैरा सी, खण्ड 10(i) केे अनुुसार इस प्रमााणपत्र कोो जारी करनेे केे प्रयोो जन सेे बैंंक ऑǛफ़ इंंडििƧया द्वाारा हमारेे समक्षș प्रस्‍‍तुु त कि�या गया था।","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c507","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":140,"text":"We have examined the relevant registers, records, forms, returns and disclosures received from the Directors of Bank of India having its Head office at Star House, C-5, `G’ Block, Bandra- Kurla Complex, Bandra (East) Mumbai 400 051 (hereinafter referred to as ‘the Bank’), produced before us by the Bank for the purpose of issuing this Certificate, in accordance with Regulation 34(3) read with Schedule V Para-C Sub clause 10(i) of the Securities Exchange Board of India (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015.\nIn our opinion and to the best of our information and according to the verifications including Directors Identification Number (DIN) status at the portal (www.mca.gov.in) as considered necessary and explanations furnished to us by the Bank & its officers, We hereby certify that none of the Directors on the Board of the Bank as stated below for the Financial Year ending on 31st March, 2026 have been debarred or disqualified from being appointed or continuing as Directors of Bank / Companies by the Securities and Exchange Board of India / Ministry of Corporate Affairs / Ministry of Finance / Reserve Bank of India or any such statutory authority.","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c508","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":140,"text":"हमारेे विƼचाार सेे तथाƫा हमारी सर्वोोत्‍‍तम जानकाारी केे अनुुसार और यथाƫा आवश्‍‍यक मानेे गए पोोर्टटल (www.mca.gov.in) पर उपलब्‍‍ध सत्‍‍यापनोंं�(नि�देेशकोंं� की पहचाान संंख्‍‍या(डीआईएन) सहि�त) एवंं बैंंक, और उसकेे अधि�ƭकारि�योंं� द्वाारा प्रस्‍‍तुु त कि�ए गए स्‍‍पष्‍‍टीीकरणोंं� केे अनुुसार हम एतद्द््वारा यह प्रमााणि�त करतेे हैंं कि� नीचेे बताायेे गए अनुुस