"document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1133","section":"Notes to Financial Statements","tag":"notes","page":336,"text":"Total Liabilities 1,089,593.04 975,699.24\nCapital Employed 22,457.00 21,378.67 20,819.91 15,613.45 24,804.19 22,436.29 0.00 (-)0.46 24,804.19 22,436.75 0.00 0.00 68,081.10 59,428.41\nUnallocated Capital 21,877.45 21,297.36\nTotal Capital\n89,958.55 80,725.78\nEmployed\nNote: Information in respect of Non-Banking subsidiaries/joint venture has been included under unallocated segment.\nबैैंक ऑҰफ़ इंडिया / BANK OF INDIA वािर््षक रिपोर््ट / Annual Report 2025-26\nPart B: Geographical Segment\nGeographical Segments Domestic International Total\nParticulars 2025-26 2024-25 2025-26 2024-25 2025-26 2024-25\nRevenue 75,475.29 70,374.04 10,174.27 10,038.41 85,649.56 80,412.45\nAssets 1,003,033.52 891,676.36 176,518.07 164,748.65 1,179,551.59 1,056,425.01\n\u0007The BOI group has recognised Business Segments as Primary reporting segment and Geographical Segments as Secondary segment in line with RBI guidelines in compliance with AS-17.\nI. Primary Segment: Business Segments\na) Treasury: ‘Treasury’ segment includes the entire investment portfolio i.e. dealing in Government and other Securities, Money Market Operations and Forex Operations including Derivative contracts.\nb) Wholesale Banking: Wholesale Banking includes all lending activities which are not included under Retail Banking.\nc) Retail Banking: Retail Banking segment comprises of Digital Banking and Other Retail Banking.","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1134","section":"Notes to Financial Statements","tag":"notes","page":337,"text":"c) Retail Banking: Retail Banking segment comprises of Digital Banking and Other Retail Banking.\nDigital Banking includes digital banking products acquired by DBUs.\nOther Retail Banking includes all housing loan accounts and borrower accounts having exposure up to ₹ 7.50.\nPricing of Inter-Segmental transfers\nRetail Banking Segment is a Primary resource mobilising unit and Wholesale Segment and Treasury Segment compensates the Retail banking segment for funds lent by it to them taking into consideration the average cost of deposits and borrowings incurred by it.\nAllocation of Assets and Liabilities:\na) Assets and Liabilities directly attributed to particular segment are allocated to the relative segment.\nb) Assets and Liabilities not directly attributable to specific segment are allocated in proportion to Earning Assets.\nAllocation of Costs:\na) Expenses directly attributed to particular segment are allocated to the relative segment.\nb) Expenses not directly attributable to specific segment are allocated in proportion to number of employees/business managed.\nII. Secondary Segment: Geographical Segments\na) Domestic Operations\nb) International Operations\nD. AS-18 “Related Party Transactions” (Parent Bank):\nI. Key Managerial Personnel:\nManaging Director & CEO: Shri Rajneesh Karnatak\nExecutive Directors: Shri P R Rajagopal\nShri Subrat Kumar\nShri Rajiv Mishra","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1135","section":"Notes to Financial Statements","tag":"notes","page":337,"text":"Shri Rajiv Mishra\nShri Pramod Kumar Dwibedi (from 24.11.2025)\nII. Remuneration paid : (Amount in ₹)\nSr No Name Designation 2025-26 2024-25\n1 Shri Rajneesh Karnatak MD & CEO 62,94,742 52,69,865\n2 Shri P. R. Rajagopal Exe. Director 68,16,348 59,42,538\n3 Shri M Karthikeyan (superannuated on 31.03.2025) Exe. Director 18,68,640 49,17,186\n4 Shri Subrat Kumar Exe. Director 76,93,522 51,40,710\n5 Shri Rajiv Mishra Exe. Director 72,54,345 35,65,716\n6 Shri Pramod Kumar Dwibedi (from 24.11.2025) Exe. Director 16,36,274 0\nबैैंक ऑҰफ़ इंडिया / BANK OF INDIA वािर््षक रिपोर््ट / Annual Report 2025-26\nIn terms of paragraph 5 of AS 18, transactions in the nature of Banker – Customer relationship, including those with Key Management Personnel and relatives of Key Management Personnel have not been disclosed, since the disclosure would conflict with Parent Bank’s duties of confidentiality.\nE. AS-19 “Leases” (Parent Bank) :\nOperating leases are cancellable at the option of the Parent Bank. The amount of lease expenses recognized in the Profit & Loss Account for such operating lease is ₹ 819.35 (Previous Year: ₹ 748.44).\nF. AS-20 “Earnings per Share” in ₹:\nSr. No. Particulars 2025-26 2024-25 1. Basic EPS 22.64 20.97 2. Diluted EPS 22.64 20.97\nCalculation of Basic & Diluted E.P.S.:\nS.No. Particulars 2025-26 2024-25","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1136","section":"Notes to Financial Statements","tag":"notes","page":338,"text":"S.No. Particulars 2025-26 2024-25\n(A) Net Profit/(Loss) for the year attributable to Equity Shareholders 10,306.30 9,548.28\n(B) Weighted Average Number of Equity shares (in crore) 455.27 455.27\n(C) Basic Earnings per Share (A/B) (₹) 22.64 20.97\n(D) Weighted Average number of Equity shares including dilutive potential equity shares ( in crore) 455.27 455.27\n(E) Dilutive Earnings per share (A/D) (₹) 22.64 20.97\n(F) Nominal Value per Equity Share (₹) 10.00 10.00\nG. AS-22 “Accounting for Taxes on Income”:\nThe Major components of Deferred Tax Assets and Deferred Tax Liabilities are as under:\nParticulars 31.03.2026 31.03.2025\nDeferred Tax Assets\nOn account of timing difference towards provisions 1164.90 2,266.96\nOthers 1338.85 936.55\nTotal Deferred Tax Assets 2503.75 3,203.51\nDeferred Tax Liabilities\nOn account of depreciation on fixed assets 157.64 179.70\nOn account of depreciation on investment 0.00 0.00\nOn account of interest accrued but not due 1054.12 957.68\nOthers 731.07 740.82\nTotal Deferred Tax Liabilities 1942.83 1,878.20\nNet Deferred Tax Assets / (Liabilities) 560.92 1,325.31\nH. AS-24 \"Discontinuing Operations\":\nThere are no discontinuing operations during the financial year 2025-26.\nI. AS-27 “Financial Reporting of Interests in Joint Ventures”:\nInvestments include ₹ 98.17 (Previous year ₹98.17) representing Parent Bank’s interest in the following jointly controlled entity:","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1137","section":"Notes to Financial Statements","tag":"notes","page":338,"text":"Investments include ₹ 98.17 (Previous year ₹98.17) representing Parent Bank’s interest in the following jointly controlled entity:\nHolding %\nSr. No. Name of the Company Amount Country of incorporation\n1. Star Union Dai–ichi Life Insurance Company Ltd. 98.17 India 27.48%\nबैैंक ऑҰफ़ इंडिया / BANK OF INDIA वािर््षक रिपोर््ट / Annual Report 2025-26\nAggregate amount of assets, liabilities, income and expenses related to the group’s interest in jointly controlled entities:\nParticulars 31.03.2026 31.03.2025\nLiabilities\nCapital & Reserves 516.41 507.62\nDeposits - -\nBorrowings 34.34 34.35\nOther Liabilities & Provisions 10,097.12 8,018.40\nTotal 10,647.87 8,560.37\nAssets\nCash and Balances with Reserve Bank of India 202.25 180.85\nBalances with Banks and Money at call and short notice - -\nInvestments 10,028.00 8,210.49\nAdvances 36.58 24.86\nFixed Assets 34.10 25.61\nOther Assets 346.94 118.56\nTotal 10,647.87 8,560.37\nCapital Commitments - -\nOther Contingent Liabilities 61.12 36.61\nIncome\nInterest Earned 26.94 24.07\nOther Income 89.90 70.87\nTotal 116.84 94.94\nExpenditure\nInterest Expended 2.66 2.66\nOperating Expenses 105.44 68.55\nProvisions & Contingencies (-)0.15 1.17\nTotal 107.95 72.38\nProfit / (Loss) 8.89 22.56\nJ. AS-28 “Impairment of Assets”:","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1138","section":"Notes to Financial Statements","tag":"notes","page":339,"text":"J. AS-28 “Impairment of Assets”:\nIn terms of Parent Bank’s approved revaluation policy, the immovable properties are revalued based on the revaluation reports of Parent Bank’s approved valuers in March 31, 2025 and the impairment of Fixed Assets year ended March 31, 2026 as per AS- 28 is “NIL”.\nK. AS-29 “Provisions, Contingent Liabilities and Contingent Assets”: (Parent Bank)\nA. Movement of Provisions for contingent liabilities\nParticulars Legal cases/contingencies*\n2025-26 2024-25\nOpening Balance 103.10 88.60\nProvided during the year 4.21 27.23\nAmounts reversed/used during the year 11.80 12.73\nClosing Balance 95.51 103.10\nTiming of outflow/uncertainties Outflow on settlement / crystallization\n*Excluding provisions for others\nबैैंक ऑҰफ़ इंडिया / BANK OF INDIA वािर््षक रिपोर््ट / Annual Report 2025-26\nB. Contingent Liabilities\nSuch liabilities are dependent upon the outcome of court order/arbitration/out of court settlement, disposal of appeals, the amount being called up, terms of contractual obligations, devolvement and raising of demand by concerned parties, as the case may be. No reimbursement is expected in such cases.\n9. Other Notes:","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1139","section":"Notes to Financial Statements","tag":"notes","page":340,"text":"9. Other Notes:\na) The investments of life insurance joint venture have been accounted for in accordance with the IRDAI guidelines instead of restating the same in accordance with the accounting policy followed by the Parent Bank. The investments of the insurance joint venture constitute approximately 3.59% (previous year 3.06%) of the total investments as on 31st March, 2026.\nb) Disclosure on amortisation of expenditure on account of enhancement in family pension of employees of the Parent Bank:\nReserve Bank of India vide its Circular No. RBI/2021-22/105 DOR.ACC.REC.57/21.04.018/2021-22 dated October 4, 2021, permitted Banks to amortise the additional liability on account of revision in family pension over a period not exceeding five years beginning with the financial year ending March 31, 2022, subject to a minimum of 1/5th of the total amount being expensed every year.\nThe Bank recognised the additional liability on account of revision in family pension amounting to ₹ 612.09 and has opted to amortise the said liability over a period not exceeding five years, beginning financial year ending March 31, 2022.","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1140","section":"Notes to Financial Statements","tag":"notes","page":340,"text":"The Bank recognised the additional liability on account of revision in family pension amounting to ₹ 612.09 and has opted to amortise the said liability over a period not exceeding five years, beginning financial year ending March 31, 2022.\nAccordingly, the Parent Bank has recognised ₹ Nil (Previous Year ₹ 41.21) as an expense in the Profit and Loss account, for the year ended March 31, 2026 towards the said additional liability and the unamortised amount of family pension liability as on the date is ₹ Nil (Previous Year ₹ Nil).\nc) Pursuant to Gazette Notification No. CG-DL-E-07042025-262329 dated April 7, 2025, the following Regional Rural Banks (RRBs), sponsored by Bank of India, have been amalgamated and the sponsor bank has been changed in respect of two RRBs with effect from May 1, 2025. The Parent Bank's investments in these RRBs are included in its financial statements as at March 31, 2025.\ni. The details of amalgamation of RRBs, where the transferee RRBs are not sponsored by Bank of India are as below:\nNew Name after Amalgamation of\nSponsor Bank of\nSr. No. Name of transferor RRBs Sponsor Bank of\ntransferee RRBs\ntransferor RRBs\nRRBs\n1 Vidharbha Konkan Gramin Bank Bank of India Maharashtra Gramin Bank Bank of Maharashtra Maharashtra Gramin Bank Bank of Maharashtra\n2 Aryavart Bank Bank of India Uttar Pradesh Gramin Bank Bank of Baroda Baroda UP Gramin Bank Bank of Baroda","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1141","section":"Notes to Financial Statements","tag":"notes","page":340,"text":"2 Aryavart Bank Bank of India Uttar Pradesh Gramin Bank Bank of Baroda Baroda UP Gramin Bank Bank of Baroda\nii. The details of amalgamation of RRBs, where the transferee RRB is sponsored by Bank of India are as below:\nNew Name after Amalgamation of\nSponsor Bank of\nSr. No. Name of transferor RRBs Sponsor Bank of\ntransferee RRBs\ntransferor RRBs\nRRBs\n1 Madhyanchal Gramin Bank State Bank of India Madhya Pradesh Gramin Bank Bank of India Madhya Pradesh Gramin Bank Bank of India\nAccordingly, during the year ended March 31, 2026, the Parent Bank has subscribed an additional amount of ₹ 329.45 towards the share capital of Madhya Pradesh Gramin Bank, being the sponsor bank of the Amalgamated RRB. During the year, the Parent Bank has received a capital redemption of ₹ 450.46 in case of Vidharbha Konkan Gramin Bank and ₹ 205.90 in case of Aryavart Bank, being the face value of its investment in the RRB.\nFurther, in case of Vidharbha Konkan Gramin Bank and Aryavart Bank, the Parent Bank has debited / credited its Consolidated Profit and Loss Account by ₹ 330.38 (Credit) and ₹ 849.18 (Debit) respectively towards reversal of difference between the carrying value of investments as on 01.05.2025 and the proceeds received for capital redemption and the same has been shown under exceptional item in the Consolidated Financial Results.","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1142","section":"Notes to Financial Statements","tag":"notes","page":340,"text":"On account of amalgamation of Madhyanchal Gramin Bank into Madhya Pradesh Gramin Bank, where the Parent Bank is the Sponsor Bank of the Amalgamated RRB, the carrying amount of bank investment in associate as on 01.05.2025 has been adjusted by ₹ 171.87 in opening Reserves and Surplus of Consolidated Financial Results, in accordance with Accounting Standard 23 - 'Accounting for Investments in Associates in Consolidated Financial Statements'.\nबैैंक ऑҰफ़ इंडिया / BANK OF INDIA वािर््षक रिपोर््ट / Annual Report 2025-26\nf) \u0007In terms of Parent Bank’s approved revaluation policy, during the year ended March 31, 2025 the immovable properties are revalued based on the revaluation reports of the Parent Bank’s approved valuers and the surplus arising from revaluation amounts to ₹1,580.24 has been added to “Revaluation Reserve”.\nd) Implementation of IFRS converged Indian Accounting Standards (Ind AS):","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1143","section":"Notes to Financial Statements","tag":"notes","page":341,"text":"d) Implementation of IFRS converged Indian Accounting Standards (Ind AS):\n\u0007RBI vide its circular DBR.BP.BC. No.29/21.07.001/2018-19 dated March 22, 2019, deferred implementation of Ind AS till further notice as the legislative amendments in Banking Regulation Act, 1949 as recommended by RBI are under consideration of the Government of India. However, RBI requires all banks to submit Proforma Ind AS Financial Statements (PFS) every half year. Accordingly, the Parent Bank has been preparing and submitting to RBI Proforma Ind AS Financial Statements (PFS) half-yearly with effect from September-2021, after seeking approval of Steering Committee formed for monitoring of implementation of Ind-AS in the Parent Bank. The PFS are also presented to Audit Committee of Board and Board for information and reporting. Recently, the RBI Vide circular No.RBI/DOR/2026-27/398 dated 27.04.2026 has issued guidelines as Reserve Bank of India (Commercial Banks – Asset Classification, Provisioning and Income Recognition) Directions, 2026 for implementation of ECL framework. The directions will be effective from 01.04.2027. The Parent Bank has already appointed the consultant for the same and is in process to implement the ECL framework.","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1144","section":"Notes to Financial Statements","tag":"notes","page":341,"text":"g) \u0007The Government of India has notified four New Labour Codes subsuming 29 legislations relating thereto effective November 21, 2025. Based on the broad assessment carried out by the management, the Parent Bank continues to comply with the major provisions having financial impact. The rules relating to said Labour Codes are yet to be notified and any resultant impact arising out of the same shall be taken care on such notification.\nh) \u0007Bank has raised Infrastructure Bonds amounting to ₹ 10,000 on December 26, 2025 at coupon rate of 7.23%.\nf) Other Income / Expenditure exceeding 1% of total income (Parent Bank)\nOther Income: Other Income includes below income exceeding 1% of the total income of the Parent Bank.\nParticulars FY 2025-26 FY 2024-25\ne) \u0007In respect of RBI referred NCLT accounts (List 1 & 2) as on March 31, 2026, the Parent Bank holds 100% provision of the aggregate outstanding value of ₹2,905.38 (Previous year ₹ 3,033.86).\n2,673.94 2,365.46\nRecovery in written off accounts\nj) Previous Year’s figures have been regrouped/ rearranged wherever considered necessary.\nºãö‡ãŠ ‚ããùû¹ãŠ ƒâãä¡¾ãã / BANK OF INDIA ÌãããäÓãÃ‡ãŠ ãäÀ¹ããñ›Ã / Annual Report 2025-26\nस्वतंंत्र लेेखाा परीीक्षʇकोंं� की रि�पोोर्टट\nसेेवा मेंं,","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1145","section":"Notes to Financial Statements","tag":"notes","page":342,"text":"सेेवा मेंं,\nबीी) \u0007उक्त तारीीख कोो समााप्त वर्षष केे लिƸए समेेकि�त लाभ हाानििƮ खातेे केे वि�वरण केे संंबंंध मेंं समूूह और उसकेे सहयोोगिƜयोंं� एवंं संंयुुक्त उद्यमोंं� केे लाभ का वास्तवि�क शेेषष; और\nबैंंक ऑҰफ़ इंंडिɇयाा केे सदस्यगणण\nसमेेकि�त वि�त्तीीय परि�णाामोंं� की लेेखाा परीीक्षाʇा पर रि�पोोर्टट\nसी) \u0007उक्त तारीीख कोो समााप्त वर्षष केे लिƸए समेेकि�त नकदीी प्रवाह वि�वरण केे माामलेे मेंं समूूह और उसकी सहयोोगी कंंपनििƮयोंं� और संं युुक्त उद्यमोंं� केे नकदीी प्रवाह का ा सही और उचििƟत वि�वरण।\nमत\n1. \u0007हमनेे बैंंक ऑ Ǜफ़ इंंडि�याा ('मूूल बैंंक') तथा�ा इसकी अनुुषंंगिƜयोंं�, सहाायक कंंपनििƮयोंं� तथा�ा संंयुुक्त उद्यमोंं� (इसकेे बाद इसेे संंयुुक्त रूप सेे 'समूूह' कहाा जाायेेगा) की लेेखा परीीक्षाșा की हैै। इसमेंं यथा�ा 31 माार्चच, 2026 कोो समेेकि�त तुुलन पत्र, समेेकि�त लाभ-हाानििƮ खाता तथा�ा संंबंंधििͳ�त वर्षष केे अंंत मेंं नकद प्रवाह की ी समेेकि�त वि�वरण तथा�ा महत्वपूूर्णण लेेखांं�कन नीीति�योंं� का सार एवंं अन्य व्याख्यात्मक जाानकाारीी सहि�त समेेकि�त वि�त्तीीय वि�वरणोंं� पर टि�प्पणि�याँँǫ शामि�ल हैंं, जि�समेंं उस ति�थि�� कोो समााप्त वर्षष केे लिƸए वि�वरणि�याँँǫ शामि�ल हैंं:\nमत का आधाɍार","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · year ended 31 March 2026","document_date":"2026-03-31","document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1146","section":"Notes to Financial Statements","tag":"notes","page":342,"text":"मत का आधाɍार\n2. \u0007हमनेे अपनी लेेखा-परीीक्षाșा, भारतीीय सनदीी लेेखाकार संं स्थाान द्वाारा जाारीी \"लेेखा-परीीक्षाșा पर माानक\" (एसए) केे अनुुसार की ी हैै। उक्त माानकोंं� केे अंंतर्गगत हमाारीी जि�म्मेेदारीी कोो वि�स्तारपूूर्ववक हमाारीी रि�पोोर्टट केे समेेकि�त वि�त्तीीय वि�वरणोंं� की लेेखापरीीक्षा